          "source_text_sha256": "5521f1bb923ecc2abd5775ad8d51961cd6c672d3a1fa5b4a4b039f5553dac2f2",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The witnesses are located around 2:15 PM on a terrace of a garden in Domessin (73) when they observe multiple small white objects moving in the sky, only visible within the sun's halo. One single testimony was collected. Of low strangeness and average consistency (two witnesses but a single testimony, no photo of PAN), this case appears to be a probable observation of insects, pollen, and/or dust passing through the sun's rays (see the investigation report). *According to the criteria of GEIPAN, consistency is the amount of reliable and objective information gathered for a testimony. Indeed, while the witnesses are in the shade, they observe the PANs within the sun's halo. Moreover, these latter are only visible in the direction of the sun. The color of the PANs and the duration of the observation are consistent with this hypothesis. The witness's mention of a \"white silver trail\" accompanying the PANs particularly suggests small spiders using the \"ballooning\" technique to move through the air. Unfortunately, the absence of other testimonies and photos of PAN does not allow for a more detailed analysis of the case and formal confirmation of the hypothesis. The case is classified as \"B\": probable observation of insects, pollen, and/or dust.",
